Observe SQL Logs
================


>>>>  N+1 Problem

You will see:

select * from customers;

select * from orders where customer_id=?;
select * from orders where customer_id=?;
select * from orders where customer_id=?;

Multiple queries.


>>>>  Batch Fetching

Instead of many queries:

select * from orders
where customer_id in (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)

Efficient batching.


>>>> FETCH JOIN Optimization

You will see:

select distinct c.*, o.*
from customers c
left join orders o
on c.id=o.customer_id;

Single optimized query.

>>>> DTO Projection

Only required columns fetched:

select c.name, count(o.id)
from customers c
left join orders o
group by c.name;



Technique					Benefit
LAZY loading			Avoid unnecessary data
FETCH JOIN				Fix N+1
DTO Projection			Less memory
Batch Fetching			Reduce SQL count

